  "query_preview": "../Tuesday through Friday/...A weaker wave will move \nnorth from Haida Gwaii Tuesday and Wednesday, providing enough \ndisturbance to generate scattered showers, mostly in the southern \npanhandle. The larger impacts may come as early as Thursday from a\nmuch deeper low. The latter low will intensify in the western \nGulf, and will have ample to mature as it looks to be held out \nover the open waters of the Gulf by some Fujiwara Effect related \nto a smaller orbiting low which most guidance has combining \ntogether.\n\nBy Friday the extent of its influence will likely reach us here \nin SEAK. Exact timing still differs between deterministic guidance\nruns. One of the larger variables being how long the two lows \norbit one another before joining and allowing the resultant low to\ntrack east. A later arrival will most likely result in a stronger\nsystem, but there is good confidence in strong gusty winds,\nespecially over coastal waters, and widespread rainfall Friday\nheading into the weekend.&&",
